Cilium v1.19.6 (chart 1.19.6), Gateway API CRDs v1.4.0
Generated 2026-08-10.

Pin rationale:
- v1.19.6 is the latest stable patch of the current stable line
  (published 2026-07-16); v1.20.0 is too fresh to pin, and 1.17/1.18 are
  older maintenance lines. 1.19.x fully supports the feature set already
  committed under cilium/:
    - CiliumGatewayClassConfig (needs >= 1.17, gateways/cilium/gateway-class-config.yaml)
    - CiliumL2AnnouncementPolicy (>= 1.16, cilium/l2-policy.yaml)
    - CiliumLoadBalancerIPPool (>= 1.16, cilium/lb-pool.yaml)
    - Gateway API (>= 1.14)

Render method (helm template, not committed binaries):
  helm template cilium cilium/cilium --version 1.19.6 \
    --namespace kube-system --include-crds \
    --set l2announcements.enabled=true \
    --set externalIPs.enabled=true \
    --set kubeProxyReplacement=true \
    --set ipam.mode=kubernetes \
    --set routingMode=native \
    --set ipv4NativeRoutingCIDR=10.244.0.0/16 \
    --set autoDirectNodeRoutes=true \
    --set endpointRoutes.enabled=true \
    --set operator.replicas=1 \
    --set gatewayAPI.enabled=true \
    --set hubble.enabled=false
  The values mirror the previous Ansible install
  (ansible/roles/cilium/tasks/main.yml:49-62). In 1.19.6 the chart no
  longer has a top-level externalIPs value (that --set was a no-op against
  1.16.x charts); external-IP handling now comes from l2announcements +
  lbipam, both enabled in the render.

Deviations from the raw chart render:
- hubble.enabled=false: k8labs does not use Hubble (no relay/UI, research
  does not touch it). Disabling it drops the two helm-rendered Secret
  objects (cilium-ca, hubble-server-certs) that contain freshly generated
  private keys — keeping the committed manifests free of secrets per
  the pinned-manifest constraints.
- No Cilium CRDs are committed: this chart ships none and the cilium-operator
  registers all cilium.io CRDs at startup
  (pkg/k8s/apis/cell.go RegisterCRDsCell, --skip-crd-creation=false).
- Gateway API CRDs are committed separately in 00-gateway-api-crds.yaml
  from kubernetes-sigs/gateway-api v1.4.0 (standard channel:
  gatewayclasses, gateways, httproutes, referencegrants). Cilium 1.19.6 is
  built against sigs.k8s.io/gateway-api v1.4.0-rc.2; the operator only
  DISCOVERS Gateway API CRDs and disables Gateway API when they are missing
  (operator/pkg/gateway-api/cell.go), so they must be applied separately.
